# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit game data.
#
# This world is developed alongside disc images, RAM dumps and save states.
# None of that belongs in a repository - it is copyrighted game content, and
# the working directory is full of it. Blanket-ignore the extensions first so
# a stray copy can never be staged by accident, then re-admit the handful of
# small blobs the world genuinely ships (its own assembled data, and the base
# patch, which is a diff rather than game content).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bin
*.iso
*.cue
*.img
*.sfc
*.smc
*.n64
*.z64
*.sav
*.srm
*.mcd
*.mcr
*.state
*.bak
!worlds/azure_dreams/data/*.bin

# Directories from the development tree, named explicitly in case any of this
# is ever copied into a wider checkout.
patches/
releases/
extracted/
ghidra/
ghidra_logs/
sharedtests/
Azure Dreams (Original)/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release artifacts. These are attached to a GitHub Release, never tracked -
# the client is a ~74 MB single-file publish that changes completely on every
# build, and git would keep every copy forever.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.apworld
*.exe
*.dll
*.zip
